  //  * limits.maxSessionTokens and softBreakRatio are MEASURED, not guessed: karvan-core closed
  //    24 checkpoints at 16.8M tokens and $13.24 each with ZERO rollovers in 30 costed sessions
  //    at 32M / 0.70 on claude-opus-5. The pair is only valid for that model - the sonnet-to-opus
  //    re-derivation was a measured 2.2x scale factor and doctor warns on neither direction.
  //    Any model change re-derives from a fresh `conductor budget` BEFORE launch (KS7.4 re-measures
  //    the lineup in edge). Cap $550 = est $424 (32 cp x $13.24) + ~29% headroom, Karvan's ratio.
  //    The 32nd checkpoint is KS10.2, the published-surface sync added on the owner's ask
  //    (ND-12); the cap moved 530 -> 550 with it rather than leaving the run to park $13 short.
  //  * FINISH-RUN 2026-08-15: KS0-KS2 and KS5 landed via workflow waves while this run sat aborted;
  //    KS3.1-3.3 landed too. The cap moved 550 -> 180 because the run's counter resumes at $42.67
  //    and only KS3.4, KS3.5, KS9 and KS10.1-2 still spend sessions (~7 cp at the measured ~$20/cp).
