      "notes": "SPEC: docs/dev/KARVANSARA-PLAN-2026-08-13.md section 6, stage KS0. This stage opens the era because the hub KS2 builds must not list a catalogue that corrupts itself: three read-only bug-list invocations under different plans grew it 22 to 31 rows on 2026-08-13, and payesh's harvest already refuses to run over one duplicate. KS0.1 keys legacy-db import on RUN ID, never plan slug, consults imported.json before importing, and ships a repair pass that collapses existing duplicates - BACK UP the catalogue before collapsing anything, and prove the payesh evidence path green on the deduped store. KS0.2 ships conductor run close and adopt verbs so a run record can be closed with provenance by CLI - the four phantom running rows and the hand-SQL procedure in .conductor/WATCH-HANDOFF.md are the acceptance; no runs UPDATE outside the store. KS0.3 is the sharp-small batch and every bug in it needs its reproduction script red then green: the gate battery must never rebuild the running engine (bug 16 - build to a shadow path), plan resolution prefers CWD over the CONDUCTOR_PLAN env var with a warning on override (bug 20 - the F0-R0 phantom stages in plans/karvan/CORE-TRACKER.md are the scar), the first-write FK error on a fresh run.db (bug 27), and the lessons.md duplicate-append regression with a pinned test."
    },
    {
