      "title": "Truth - every read surface reconciles",
      "sessions": 6,
      "ownerGate": false,
      "kind": "deliver",
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/dev/KARVANSARA-PLAN-2026-08-13.md section 6, stage KS1 - the 2026-08-07 verified plan's Epic 1 with its corrected scopes, absorbed not re-litigated; read docs/dev/NEXT-ERA-VERIFIED-PLAN-2026-08-07.md Epic 1 for the per-checkpoint detail. The invariant this stage installs: the event fold is truth, side-tables are views, and every external reader reconciles. KS1.1 makes a plan reload update the run row with limits provenance labeled at-launch versus now. KS1.2 derives stage rows from the fold and retires stages side-table reads - RunArchive.Checkpoints is the template; an architecture test forbids readers of stages.session_count. KS1.3 is render-time liveness reconciliation in history, the fleet list and json output - a killed engine's run must never list as running; this closes the read half of FU-F1-06 and KS0.2 was the write half. KS1.4 lands the doctor plan-semantics lints: gate-command path probe, checkpoint-id versus tracker cross-check, hook dry-run, plan drift, composed-prompt argv-length check for the 8191-char Windows ceiling (bugs 15 and 21), brace sweep, and the escalation-token sweep over notes and templates - doctor must go red on each of seven seeded trap plans. KS1.5 rewrites the ARCHITECTURE.md rollback paragraph to match ControlDispatcher and pins it with a docs-match-reality test. KS1.6 states the invariant as an architecture test: readers outside the engine may not consume mutable snapshot columns that have a fold-derived equivalent."
