      "title": "The open door - bare conductor is the app, and every section reads",
      "sessions": 8,
      "ownerGate": false,
      "kind": "deliver",
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/dev/KARVANSARA-PLAN-2026-08-13.md section 6, stage KS2. Face work obeys face-go/STYLE.md and adr 0006 - pad plain text then style, clamp with MaxWidth and MaxHeight, goldens pinned UTC under face-go/internal/tui/testdata/golden and regenerated only in a separate rebaseline commit. KS2.1: bare conductor on a TTY resolves the machine state home and opens the hub - recent runs live and past reconciled, plans discovered here, actions attach start plan-new history; non-TTY prints a status board and exits 0; every existing verb and --help unchanged. KS2.2: a read-only control-plane mode over the state home so the Face attaches to FINISHED runs - sessions, money, timeline, report render with no engine process. KS2.3: start a run from the hub - choose plan, journey preview, launch a DETACHED engine with stderr redirected (the field log's hard-won launch shape becomes the code path), then attach; killing the Face must leave the engine alive. KS2.4: one picker merging fleet probe and catalogue - live runs attach, past runs open read-only, across repos, write tokens never crossing runs. KS2.5: conductor status with no resolvable plan prints a machine-level board, never the multiple-plan-files error. KS2.6: park hygiene - a park emits once, notifier rate-limited with a max per incident, dry-run never notifies, a monitor listing verb; replay the 2026-08-02 escalation-token incident and demand exactly one notification. KS2.7: LONG TEXT SCROLLS EVERYWHERE - finish adr 0006 adoption: Agent console and transcript, Kanban detail, History, Telegram feed and Processes each own a pane viewport; delete the last hand-rolled scroll integers such as consoleScroll in tab_agent.go, applyPaneScroll the only key path; a module-intent test forbids new bespoke scroll fields; glitch-sweep proves a 500-line body scrolls to its end in every tab. KS2.8: THE READER - one full-screen overlay opens any truncated cell or row (checkpoint note, evidence text, session result, gate output, telegram message): soft-wrapped prose, the adr pager keys, percent readout, themed markdown where the body is markdown, esc back; a 2000-line report and a 300-char kanban note both readable to the last line at 80x24."
    },
    {
      "id": "KS3",
      "title": "Authoring - no human writes JSON",
      "sessions": 5,
      "ownerGate": false,
      "kind": "deliver",
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/dev/KARVANSARA-PLAN-2026-08-13.md section 6, stage KS3, and the per-checkpoint contract plans/karvansara/contracts/KS3.json - the acceptance and proofs there are the bar. STATE AT HANDOVER (2026-08-15): KS3.1, KS3.2 and KS3.3 are DONE - delivered and adversarially verified in the wave era, merged on feat/karvansara (commits 60101eb, 106637b plus fb37c83, 985bdf4) - do not redo them. KS3.4's verb EXISTS: conductor preflight, six legs, one verdict (31857ce plus eight fix commits), but the checkpoint was REFUTED SEVEN ROUNDS, every round one class of defect - the compose leg's decision stops before the session the real launch spawns, so the drill answers READY while conductor run composes a real agent session. Round-7 findings verbatim, with live reproduction rigs: plans/karvansara/contracts/ks3-4-round7-findings.json and plans/karvansara/contracts/ks3-4-v7-rigs/ (each rig needs its own state home, explicit -p, CONDUCTOR_PLAN cleared, and YOUR FRESH BUILD, never the PATH engine). Three branches remain wrong: gate-or-audit scheduling (StageSelection stops at ScheduleGateOrAudit and RunLoop re-decides into an Audit session the headline denies), completion-confirm (a red required gate queues a Fix session while the drill says the launch confirms completion), and the queued phase gate (same mechanism, Fix session). ROUND-8 DIRECTION, decided at lane close: lift the gate-or-audit scheduling branch into the shared pure decision the way QueuesParallelAuditFix was lifted, so NextAction carries the decision THROUGH the scheduling to the session it produces; make the completion and phase-gate headlines honest - that launch runs a battery first and a red one composes a Fix session, say so; and point the round-6 store-backed LiveSessionAsync harness in tests/Conductor.Tests/KS3_4PreflightTests.cs at all three branches, each new fact proven red against the pre-fix code first. The park branch already got exactly this treatment (commit b8a6002) - it is the pattern to follow. THEN KS3.5 (second cut line): import bridges per the contract - spec-kit tasks.md, Task-Master tasks.json, plain markdown checklist to plan; the spec-kit sample must convert and drive conductor demo to completion."
    },
    {
