      "notes": "SPEC: docs/dev/KARVANSARA-PLAN-2026-08-13.md section 6, stage KS5 - the verified plan's Epic 2 plus the uncounted paths. Billed-money-only is the house rule: no price table may appear in any diff. KS5.1: a machine-wide ledger verb answering what this machine spent this week or month, across the catalogue, cross-checked against per-run money output. KS5.2: lane, advisor and supervisor spend counted - cost rows for every spawned model process, caps see them, the advisor's flat seconds-based estimate replaced by billed rows where the provider reports; the architecture test is that any process-spawning path that takes a model must write a costs row. KS5.3: BudgetAnalyzer prescriptions surfaced at plan-reload - a reload whose ceiling contradicts the measured floor logs the disagreement at the boundary. KS5.4: approve and cap semantics - approve on a budget park RAISES THE CEILING EXPLICITLY with the amount stated instead of resetting the counter to zero, and the cap check runs after the queued reload applies; replay the field-log 2026-07-29 19:03 incident and demand no silent double-spend."
    },
    {
      "id": "KS9",
      "title": "The far door - GitHub is the remotest view",
      "sessions": 3,
      "ownerGate": false,
      "kind": "deliver",
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/dev/GITHUB-SYNC-DESIGN-2026-08-13.md - the committed design, executed as decided: ONE-WAY push, OFF BY DEFAULT, NOTHING INBOUND, the tracker stays the verified contract, two-way sync is a rejected non-goal (L6.3, D-7, ADR 0005 spirit). All live proofs go to a SCRATCH GitHub repo - never post to shaahink/conductor or any real repo during this stage; the owner does the first real backfill at KS10.3. Token comes from the new SecretsStore field or the CONDUCTOR_GITHUB_TOKEN override; raw HttpClient on the ReleaseClient pattern, no Octokit. KS9.1: token plumbing, the client, and conductor github sync --backfill posting a FINISHED run's board - one issue per TaskItem with upsert-never-clobber and retire-dont-delete semantics - plus its diary as a run issue with one comment per SessionFinished; re-running the backfill must mint zero duplicates. KS9.2: the live mirror - a reconciler over IRunStore.ReadEventsAfter, never a hot IEventSink, batched and network-failure-proof; kill the network mid-run and the run is unharmed while the board converges on reconnect; replay from cursor zero produces zero duplicates. KS9.3 (cut line inside this stage): Projects v2 board via GraphQL mirroring stage status - it needs the project scope the owner's gh token lacks; if the one-time gh auth refresh has not happened, report the precise refusal and leave the checkpoint SKIPPED rather than half-done. PER-CHECKPOINT CONTRACT: plans/karvansara/contracts/KS9-10.json - the acceptance and proofs there are the bar. Facts verified 2026-08-15: gh is authenticated as shaahink with repo and delete_repo scopes and WITHOUT the project scope, so KS9.3's precise-refusal SKIPPED outcome is the expected one unless the owner grants the scope mid-run. For live proofs create or reuse a PRIVATE scratch repo named conductor-sync-scratch under the shaahink account via gh repo create; a token for the CONDUCTOR_GITHUB_TOKEN override can be read from gh auth token."
    },
    {
      "id": "KS10",
      "title": "Ship core",
      "sessions": 3,
      "ownerGate": true,
      "kind": "deliver",
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/dev/KARVANSARA-PLAN-2026-08-13.md section 6, stage KS10 - the Karvan K7 pattern, plus decision ND-12 which split the published surface out of KS10.1 because a docs clause buried in a ship checkpoint is how doc drift survives an era. KS10.1 is the INTERNAL record: reconcile ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/dev with the engine for everything this plan changed; a closure ledger naming every bug and followup row closed here or its living owner; re-run conductor budget and write this run's own figures into TOKEN-BUDGET-TUNING - that number is what karvansara-edge compiles against, and if the prescription disagrees with this plan's estimate the prescription wins and the plan doc gets corrected in place. KS10.2 is the PUBLISHED surface and it is the checkpoint the owner asked for by name: README.md first, because KS2.1 changes the very first command a reader runs; then the docs user set - cli.md, operating.md, quickstart.md, troubleshooting.md, tracker.md, plan-config.md and the docs/README.md index; then .github issue and PR templates wherever a verb changed; then the Unreleased section of CHANGELOG.md written as the release body the world reads, because release.yml refuses a tag whose section is missing and uses that section verbatim - the CHANGELOG is the GitHub sync for humans exactly as KS9 is the sync for machines. The durable half is a test, not a promise: extend SF7_1DocsMatchRealityTests so every verb this era adds and every command README quotes is pinned, and prove it goes red on a seeded stale doc. Last, the field guide: payesh lives at C:/code/conductor-site and its harvest reads the run store KS0.1 rewrote, so re-run that harvest against the deduped catalogue as the end-to-end proof KS0.1 did not break its most public consumer - commit it on a branch and open a PR, NEVER push to the live site from a session, and if the harvest cannot run for a reason outside this plan record the precise refusal in the closure ledger and leave that half SKIPPED. KS10.3 is OWNER-ONLY: merge feat/karvansara to master, tag the release through the existing pipeline with KS10.2's CHANGELOG section as the body, reinstall with the reported version matching the releases page - the FIRST install of this run, only after the owner confirms no other conductor run is live on this machine - then the era's closing act, conductor github sync --backfill of THIS run, the first real use of KS9 on the run that built it, and merge the payesh PR so the field guide matches the shipped engine. PER-CHECKPOINT CONTRACT: plans/karvansara/contracts/KS9-10.json - the acceptance and proofs there are the bar. KS10.1's closure ledger inherits three named gaps from the KS5 lane close: the face tokens-cap row still quotes the plan-file ceiling; approve lost CtlCommand's yes and force flags; and one owner-gate-plus-lowered-cap path spends a session before parking."
    }
